  "description": "A custom emoji (SPEC §12.2, §16.9). The blob is the image encrypted with AES-128-GCM under its own 16-byte key, with an all-zero 12-byte nonce and no associated data, as files are (§14); its length is size + 16. The record is a `signed` object with t = \"community-emoji\", signed by device 1 of fork.json (k = its Ed25519 component), whose body is {community, blob, sha256: of the blob, size: of the plaintext, head, ts, by, emoji}. emoji is a `sealed`: key = SHA-256 of the community metadata key, ct = a 12-byte nonce, then AES-128-GCM of JCS(emoji-secret) under HKDF-Expand(metadata key, \"tieroute community metadata\", 16), with the associated data JCS([\"tieroute community emoji\", community, blob]), both as unpadded base64url. The community identifier, blob ID, head, and nonce are stand-ins. emoji_ref is what a message's custom-emoji carries for :night_owl:.",
